{{!
    @template report_competency/user_course_navigation

    Jump to another participant or filter by an activity on the breakdown report, overridden by Dimensions.

    Mirrors report_competency/user_course_navigation of Moodle 5.3 (2026100500),
    report/competency/templates/user_course_navigation.mustache. Re-diff it against that file on every
    core upgrade.

    Kept from core, because report_competency/user_course_navigation and core/form-autocomplete read
    them: the selects' ids user-nav-<uniqid> and module-nav-<uniqid> and their labels (core's Behat
    sets the activity filter through its label, "Filter competencies by resource or activity"), every
    option with its value and selected state, the form's class user-competency-course-navigation
    (tool_lp's stylesheet hides the native selects under it; the autocomplete draws in their place), the
    hidden fields user, id and mod, the
    group selector (core's own HTML, triple-stashed) and the JavaScript itself. The names keep core's
    double stash.
    Changed: the panel is the theme's (dim-comp-nav); the group selector sits in a div rather than a
    paragraph, because core's single_select markup is a form, which a paragraph cannot hold.
    The JavaScript is core's statement for statement, with the constructor's parameter capitalised
    (Nav) and long lines wrapped, for the template lint a plugin's templates go through and core's do not.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * groupselector - HTML
    * userid, courseid, moduleid, baseurl - read by the JavaScript and the hidden fields
    * hasusers - boolean
    * users - array of id, selected, fullname
    * hasmodules - boolean
    * modules - array of id, selected, name

    Example context (json):
    {
        "groupselector": "",
        "userid": 3,
        "courseid": 2,
        "moduleid": 0,
        "baseurl": "https://example.com/report/competency/index.php",
        "hasusers": true,
        "users": [
            {"id": 3, "fullname": "Sam Student", "selected": true},
            {"id": 4, "fullname": "Robin Learner", "selected": false}
        ],
        "hasmodules": true,
        "modules": [
            {"id": 0, "name": "All activities", "selected": true},
            {"id": 5, "name": "Case study", "selected": false}
        ]
    }
}}
<div class="dim-comp-nav float-end">
{{#groupselector}}
<div class="dim-comp-nav__group">{{{groupselector}}}</div>
{{/groupselector}}
<form class="user-competency-course-navigation">
<input type="hidden" name="user" value="{{userid}}">
<input type="hidden" name="id" value="{{courseid}}">
<input type="hidden" name="mod" value="{{moduleid}}">
{{#hasusers}}
<span class="dim-comp-nav__group">
<label for="user-nav-{{uniqid}}" class="accesshide">{{#str}}jumptouser, tool_lp{{/str}}</label>
<select id="user-nav-{{uniqid}}">
{{#users}}
<option value="{{id}}" {{#selected}}selected="selected"{{/selected}}>{{fullname}}</option>
{{/users}}
</select>
</span>
{{/hasusers}}

{{#hasmodules}}
<span class="dim-comp-nav__group">
<label for="module-nav-{{uniqid}}" class="accesshide">{{#str}}filterbyactivity, tool_lp{{/str}}</label>
<select id="module-nav-{{uniqid}}">
{{#modules}}
<option value="{{id}}" {{#selected}}selected="selected"{{/selected}}>{{name}}</option>
{{/modules}}
</select>
</span>
{{/hasmodules}}
</form>
</div>
{{#js}}
require(['core/form-autocomplete', 'report_competency/user_course_navigation'], function(autocomplete, Nav) {
    (new Nav('#user-nav-{{uniqid}}', '#module-nav-{{uniqid}}',
        '{{baseurl}}', {{userid}}, {{courseid}}, {{moduleid}}));
{{#hasusers}}
    autocomplete.enhance('#user-nav-{{uniqid}}', false, false, {{# quote }}{{# str }}jumptouser, tool_lp{{/ str }}{{/ quote }});
{{/hasusers}}
{{#hasmodules}}
    autocomplete.enhance('#module-nav-{{uniqid}}', false, false, {{# quote }}{{# str }}filterbyactivity, tool_lp{{/ str }}{{/ quote }});
{{/hasmodules}}
});
{{/js}}
